Python 3 Development Installation
=================================

This is a development-only installation procedure for the ongoing
migration of TMDA 1.1.12. It is not a production release.

Validated environments
----------------------

The GitHub Actions workflow python3-install.yml installs the package
inside a clean virtual environment with Python 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14
on Ubuntu. FreeBSD deployment is not yet verified.

Linux or FreeBSD test environment
---------------------------------

Use a non-privileged account and a disposable test directory. Do
not replace an existing TMDA installation or use a live MTA.

    git clone https://github.com/kmansur/tmda.git
    cd tmda
    git switch feature/python3-migration

    python3.12 -m venv .venv
    .venv/bin/python -m pip install --upgrade pip
    .venv/bin/python -m pip install .

    .venv/bin/tmda-address -V
    .venv/bin/tmda-keygen -V
    .venv/bin/tmda-ofmipd --help

The environment must provide the selected Python interpreter and
its virtual environment support. Python 3.13 or 3.14 may be used in place of Python 3.12.

Python 3 package metadata
-------------------------

pyproject.toml installs the original TMDA package and nine
command-line executables. The historical package version remains
1.1.12; the metadata clearly identifies the build as a development
migration. The historical Python 2 copy of the email package is
not included in the installed Python 3 package.

The migration retains original copyright notices and GPL terms.

Development validation
----------------------

The current CI includes compilation of all extensionless executables,
cryptographic and compatibility tests, isolated SMTP/TLS loopback
transactions, message queue tests and a clean virtual environment
installation. These tests do not certify production delivery.

Do not use this branch for a production mail gateway until real MTA
integration, timeout and failure recovery, resource limits, sustained
load and security review have been completed.
